# Natas Level 8 → Level 9

### Challenge

**URL: http://natas8.natas.labs.overthewire.org/**

Clicking "View sourcecode" reveals the following PHP function used to hide the secret:

```
<?

$encodedSecret = "3d3d516343746d4d6d6c315669563362";

function encodeSecret($secret) {
    return bin2hex(strrev(base64_encode($secret)));
}

if(array_key_exists("submit", $_POST)) {
    if(encodeSecret($_POST['secret']) == $encodedSecret) {
    print "Access granted. The password for natas9 is <censored>";
    } else {
    print "Wrong secret";
    }
}
?>
```

### Walkthrough

1.  The `encodeSecret` function performs three operations in this specific order:
  1. `base64_encode($secret)`
  2. `strrev()` (reverses the string)
  3. `bin2hex()` (converts binary data to hexadecimal)
2.  To recover the original secret, apply the inverse functions in reverse order:
  1. `hex2bin()` (convert hex back to binary/string)
  2. `strrev()` (reverse the string back)
  3. `base64_decode()` (decode Base64)
3.  Run this logic in PHP to decode it:
  ```
  <?php
  $encoded = "3d3d516343746d4d6d6c315669563362";
  $step1 = hex2bin($encoded);
  $step2 = strrev($step1);
  $step3 = base64_decode($step2);  // Result: "oubWYf2kBq"
  echo $step3;
  ?>
  ```
4.  Enter `oubWYf2kBq` into the input field on the Natas 8 page and click **Submit**.
  ![alt text](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/azkbrqlna/OverTheWire-Walkthrough/main/Natas/images/image-22.png)

